        {
          "id": 3068263001,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "> Programs that read one file and write out another file, with some processing in between, have a different path, so those programs, e.g. TShark and editcap, don't need it.\n\nEditcap doesn't do dissection, so it won't find any secrets to inject.\n\nTShark can do dissection; the change to *its* path would, I think:\n\n- with one-pass processing, involve the code path checking, before writing the packet, whether any new secrets have been added and writing out a DSB for them, if the output capture file format supports it;\n- with two-pass processing, just involve the second pass writing out any secrets that have been added to the file.\n\nThe latter of those may already work; the former of those probably doesn't. In *either* case, those would be enhancements if changes were made to make them work, so it's not as if they'd be broken without this change.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
